Exactly. Once you strip away the animal’s details, you get a strategy invariant: a compact move that keeps working across changing situations.

* Crocodile: outlast underwater + bite hard
* Spider: trap prey + move safely through your own trap
* Remora: attach to power + let it carry you
* Leafcutter ant: turn scraps into a food system

The body is one implementation; the strategy is the reusable pattern. Then you can look for the same invariant in people, tools, organizations, or markets—and test where it transfers.